    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "I published an article titled, “Linguistic Diversity in Libraries” in the July 10, 2018 edition of Library Journal. I am taking a light-hearted approach to this subject because I do not believe that diversity discussions always have to be so serious. In the words of a great philosopher, the Joker, “Why so serious?” Now more than ever, we can all use a bit of levity. As a result, this posting includes a crossword puzzle to test your vernacular fluency. All terminology for answers to the crossword puzzle is on the Urban Dictionary website. For the uninitiated, I added clues, in parentheses, containing the answer’s number and either “A” for Across or “D” for Down.",
